{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "pm2-interval-hydraulic-press",
  "title": "PM-2 interval for hydraulic presses",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "ee8c85b3-52a4-4bf5-a820-822e346e0bc5",
      "question": "What PM-2 interval does the preventive maintenance manual set for a hydraulic press, and how often is its hydraulic oil sampled?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-03T04:15:07.466356Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-03T04:15:11.463982Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Based on the preventive maintenance manual (PM-MAN-001, Rev D), here are the details for hydraulic presses:\n\n| Item | Interval |\n|------|----------|\n| **PM-2 interval** | **60 calendar days** [1] |\n| **Hydraulic oil sampling** | **Every 90 days** [1] |\n\nThe manual's Table 1 specifies that hydraulic presses have a PM-2 interval of 60 calendar days, and their fluid/lubricant analysis calls for a hydraulic oil sample every 90 days. The PM-2 task list for hydraulic presses also includes taking a hydraulic oil sample for particle count and water content, and replacing return filters during each PM-2 service.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — 2 documents — evidence `hermes-receipt:0204e1d854b130d81eb8cb1766cd4400e962a61f4a818a70a9047da91e51a576`",
