                "snippet": "Preventive Maintenance Manual\n3. Maintenance levels\n4. Maintenance intervals by machine type\nTable 1 gives the PM-2 interval for each machine type. The interval is counted in calendar days from the date of the last completed PM-2 on that machine. Weekends and plant holidays count as days.\nCNC Mill, PM-1 operator check = Daily. CNC Mill, PM-2 interval (calendar days) = 90. CNC Mill, Fluid and lubricant analysis = Coolant concentration and pH weekly. CNC Mill, Geometry and calibration = Ballbar circularity check at every PM-2. CNC Lathe, PM-1 operator check = Daily. CNC Lathe, PM-2 interval (calendar days) = 120. CNC Lathe, Fluid and lubricant analysis = Coolant concentration and pH weekly. CNC Lathe, Geometry and calibration = Chuck runout and turret indexing at every PM-2. Hydraulic Press, PM-1 operator check = Daily. Hydraulic Press, PM-2 interval (calendar days) = 60. Hydraulic Press, Fluid and lubricant analysis = Hydraulic oil sample every 90 days. Hydraulic Press, Geometry and calibration = Platen parallelism at every second PM-2. Robot Cell, PM-1 operator check = Weekly. Robot Cell, PM-2 interval (calendar days) = 180. Robot Cell, Fluid and lubricant analysis = Reducer grease sample at every PM-2. Robot Cell, Geometry and calibration = Tool center point calibration at every PM-2. Surface Grinder, PM-1 operator check = Daily. Surface Grinder, PM-2 interval (calendar days) = 90. Surface Grinder, Fluid and lubricant analysis = Coolant concentration weekly. Surface Grinder,",
