                "snippet": "Preventive Maintenance Manual\n3. Maintenance levels\n4. Maintenance intervals by machine type\n- A PM-2 is due when the number of days since the machine’s last completed PM-2 reaches the interval in Table 1, and overdue when it exceeds that interval.\n- A corrective repair does not restart the PM-2 clock, even when the repair replaces a component that PM-2 would have inspected.\n- A PM-2 started on one day and finished on the next is dated by the day it started.\n- For a new machine the clock starts at its commissioning date and runs until its first PM-2 is completed.\n- Planners should book each PM-2 two to nine days before its due date so that a short slip does not make the machine overdue.\nSynthetic document for a software demonstration. Not for operational use. Page 2\nATLAS PRECISION COMPONENTS PM-MAN-001 | Rev D",
